# AI Performance Engineering - Blackwell Requirements
# Target: Blackwell B200 (SM100) with PyTorch 2.9.1+cu130, CUDA 13.0, Triton 3.5.1
# All versions are pinned to exact versions for reproducible builds. The ABI-bound
# vLLM CUDA 13 wheel is intentionally installed separately with --no-deps from
# vllm_no_deps.pin; resolving its upstream ray[cgraph] extra would install the
# CUDA 12 CuPy distribution beside the CUDA 13 CuPy distribution required here.
# uv.lock contains only the repository's Python compatibility metadata. It is
# not a resolved dependency lock. This file remains the environment source.
#
# GB300 / Blackwell Ultra (sm_103) note (verified 2026-06-09): the validated, working
# GB300 toolchain is the NGC torch 2.12 base (CUDA 13; arch_list sm_100 + compute_120,
# which forward-compat JITs onto sm_103) PLUS the source fixes in docs/gb300-runbook.md.
# Two pins do NOT help GB300: (a) torch==2.9.1+cu130 fails to import on sm_103 hosts
# (ModuleNotFoundError: torch._opaque_base); (b) triton==3.5.0 still aborts sm_103
# max-autotune (LLVM cannot select tcgen05.wait.st) with torch 2.12, same as triton 3.7
# -- so the max-autotune->default fallback guard is required regardless of triton version.
# See docs/gb300-runbook.md "Toolchain GB300-readiness". The 2.9.1 pin is the B200 baseline.

# Core PyTorch ecosystem (CUDA 13 wheels)
# Resolution evidence omits absent local find-links; all base specs remain.
--extra-index-url https://download.pytorch.org/whl/cu130
# Resolve the exact +cu130 torch pin below from the official stable CUDA index.
# Keep PyPI available for the remaining packages and local wheels when present.
# torchvision and torchaudio are installed with the matched CUDA stack.

# PyTorch 2.9.1 CUDA wheel metadata requires this exact Linux dependency.
triton==3.5.1

